select b.id,51,null,$q$A bicycle racing track is a level circular road of radius 10 m. Three cyclists P, Q and R with identical cycles are cycling on the track with speeds 2 m/s, 3 m/s and 5 m/s respectively. If the coefficient of friction between the tyres and the road is 0.1, then which cyclist will slip? (Take g = 10 m/s²)$q$,$q$P only$q$,$q$Q only$q$,$q$R only$q$,$q$All will slip$q$,0.98,'{}'::text[],$q$NDA_II_2026_GK_051$q$,$q$A bicycle racing track is a level circular road of radius 10 m. Three cyclists P, Q and R with identical cycles are cycling on the track with speeds 2 m/s, 3 m/s and 5 m/s respectively. If the coefficient of friction between the tyres and the road is 0.1, then which cyclist will slip? (Take g = 10 m/s²)$q$,$q$P only$q$,$q$Q only$q$,$q$R only$q$,$q$All will slip$q$,$q$95a7a0af38eccd222ab01a43a99e9c8745a68fc55159d4abbde063d383c25bac$q$,$q$C$q$,'MODEL_ONLY',$q$dp-solved://NDA_2026_II_GAT_GK_SET_A$q$,null,$q$C$q$,$q$C$q$,false,$q$Science & Technology$q$,$q$Physics$q$,$q$Classical Mechanics, Motion & Gravitation$q$,$q$Maximum speed on a flat circular track$q$,'Knowledge',$q$Single MCQ$q$,$q$PATTERN.DIRECT$q$,$q$Concept: friction supplies the centripetal force, so the maximum safe speed is $v_{max}=\sqrt{\mu rg}$.
Step 1: $v_{max}=\sqrt{0.1\times10\times10}=\sqrt{10}\approx3.16$ m/s.
Step 2: P (2) and Q (3) are below this; R (5) is above, so only R slips.
