select b.id,58,null,$q$A fish is at a depth d in water of refractive index 4/3. If a transparent slab of refractive index 3/2 and thickness d/2 is placed on the surface of water, then which one of the following is the apparent depth of the fish as observed by an observer in air?$q$,$q$d/2$q$,$q$5d/8$q$,$q$13d/12$q$,$q$17d/24$q$,0.98,'{}'::text[],$q$NDA_II_2026_GK_058$q$,$q$A fish is at a depth d in water of refractive index 4/3. If a transparent slab of refractive index 3/2 and thickness d/2 is placed on the surface of water, then which one of the following is the apparent depth of the fish as observed by an observer in air?$q$,$q$d/2$q$,$q$5d/8$q$,$q$13d/12$q$,$q$17d/24$q$,$q$bfe90ce3029ed32740945e1226836767c219935f99a166de939f4bb46e224b2a$q$,$q$C$q$,'MODEL_ONLY',$q$dp-solved://NDA_2026_II_GAT_GK_SET_A$q$,null,$q$C$q$,$q$C$q$,false,$q$Science & Technology$q$,$q$Physics$q$,$q$Geometrical & Physical Optics$q$,$q$Apparent depth through layered media$q$,'Knowledge',$q$Single MCQ$q$,$q$PATTERN.DIRECT$q$,$q$Concept: apparent depth of each layer = real thickness / refractive index.
Step 1: water layer: $\frac{d}{4/3}=\frac{3d}4$.
Step 2: slab: $\frac{d/2}{3/2}=\frac d3$.
Step 3: total $=\frac{3d}4+\frac d3=\frac{13d}{12}$.
Answer: (c)$q$,$q$NDA II 2026 General Ability Test Part B (English side)$q$,false,array['format:single_mcq','key:dp_solved'],$q$Static$q$,42.25,$q$Moderate$q$,0.97,0.85,0.85,false,'ENRICHED','INCLUDE',$q$Apparent depth through layered media$q$,$q$COMP.SNT.PHYSICS$q$,$q$SRC.NCERT.SCIENCE$q$,$q$TEMP.STATIC$q$,80,90,100,60,57.75,0,0,0,0,$q${"answer_audit": {"authority": "DP_SOLVED_INTERNAL", "note": "Not an official UPSC key"}, "source_explanation_evidence": {"captured": true, "provider": "DP internal solved key", "text": "Concept: apparent depth of each layer = real thickness / refractive index.\nStep 1: water layer: $\\frac{d}{4/3}=\\frac{3d}4$.\nStep 2: slab: $\\frac{d/2}{3/2}=\\frac d3$.\nStep 3: total $=\\frac{3d}4+\\frac d3=\\frac{13d}{12}$.\nAnswer: (c)"}}$q$::jsonb from b
union all
