select b.id,64,null,$q$A biconvex lens is made of a material of refractive index 2 such that the ratio of the radii of curvature of its two faces is 1 : 2. A point source in air is placed on the principal axis of this lens at a distance u from the lens. Which one of the following is correct if the image is formed exactly at the same distance as that of the point source? (where R is the radius of curvature of the first face)$q$,$q$u = R$q$,$q$u = 2R$q$,$q$2u = 3R$q$,$q$3u = 4R$q$,0.98,'{}'::text[],$q$NDA_II_2026_GK_064$q$,$q$A biconvex lens is made of a material of refractive index 2 such that the ratio of the radii of curvature of its two faces is 1 : 2. A point source in air is placed on the principal axis of this lens at a distance u from the lens. Which one of the following is correct if the image is formed exactly at the same distance as that of the point source? (where R is the radius of curvature of the first face)$q$,$q$u = R$q$,$q$u = 2R$q$,$q$2u = 3R$q$,$q$3u = 4R$q$,$q$c58bcd17e1fdec74c8c2d4882ab4d13392729714bfb2f0cabbd14778ed59ce83$q$,$q$D$q$,'MODEL_ONLY',$q$dp-solved://NDA_2026_II_GAT_GK_SET_A$q$,null,$q$D$q$,$q$D$q$,false,$q$Science & Technology$q$,$q$Physics$q$,$q$Geometrical & Physical Optics$q$,$q$Lens maker's formula and image distance$q$,'Knowledge',$q$Single MCQ$q$,$q$PATTERN.DIRECT$q$,$q$Step 1: $\frac1f=(2-1)\left(\frac1R+\frac1{2R}\right)=\frac3{2R}\Rightarrow f=\frac{2R}3$.
Step 2: image at the same distance as the object means $u=v=2f=\frac{4R}3$.
So $3u=4R$.
Answer: (d)$q$,$q$NDA II 2026 General Ability Test Part B (English side)$q$,false,array['format:single_mcq','key:dp_solved'],$q$Static$q$,62,$q$Hard$q$,0.97,0.85,0.85,false,'ENRICHED','INCLUDE',$q$Lens maker's formula and image distance$q$,$q$COMP.SNT.PHYSICS$q$,$q$SRC.NCERT.SCIENCE$q$,$q$TEMP.STATIC$q$,80,90,100,60,38,0,0,0,0,$q${"answer_audit": {"authority": "DP_SOLVED_INTERNAL", "note": "Not an official UPSC key"}, "source_explanation_evidence": {"captured": true, "provider": "DP internal solved key", "text": "Step 1: $\\frac1f=(2-1)\\left(\\frac1R+\\frac1{2R}\\right)=\\frac3{2R}\\Rightarrow f=\\frac{2R}3$.\nStep 2: image at the same distance as the object means $u=v=2f=\\frac{4R}3$.\nSo $3u=4R$.\nAnswer: (d)"}}$q$::jsonb from b
