select b.id,71,null,$q$Three parallel glass slabs of refractive indices 1.5, √3 and 1.5 respectively have widths 2 mm, 1 mm and 4 mm. The combination is in air. Light is incident at the first slab at an angle of incidence π/3. What is the angle with respect to the normal at which the light will emerge from the final surface?$q$,$q$π/6$q$,$q$π/4$q$,$q$π/3$q$,$q$π/12$q$,0.98,'{}'::text[],$q$NDA_II_2026_GK_071$q$,$q$Three parallel glass slabs of refractive indices 1.5, √3 and 1.5 respectively have widths 2 mm, 1 mm and 4 mm. The combination is in air. Light is incident at the first slab at an angle of incidence π/3. What is the angle with respect to the normal at which the light will emerge from the final surface?$q$,$q$π/6$q$,$q$π/4$q$,$q$π/3$q$,$q$π/12$q$,$q$f9ec45feba55f335f37d4fefa3988f53a2c787795fe94439a6ac33eb839f0bb1$q$,$q$C$q$,'MODEL_ONLY',$q$dp-solved://NDA_2026_II_GAT_GK_SET_A$q$,null,$q$C$q$,$q$C$q$,false,$q$Science & Technology$q$,$q$Physics$q$,$q$Geometrical & Physical Optics$q$,$q$Refraction through parallel slabs$q$,'Knowledge',$q$Single MCQ$q$,$q$PATTERN.DIRECT$q$,$q$Concept: by Snell's law across parallel faces, $n_1\sin\theta_1=n_2\sin\theta_2=\dots$, so the product $n\sin\theta$ is constant.
The light starts and ends in air, so the emergent angle equals the incident angle, $\frac\pi3$ (no total internal reflection occurs inside since $\sin\theta<1$ in every slab).
Answer: (c)$q$,$q$NDA II 2026 General Ability Test Part B (English side)$q$,false,array['format:single_mcq','key:dp_solved'],$q$Static$q$,42.25,$q$Moderate$q$,0.97,0.85,0.85,false,'ENRICHED','INCLUDE',$q$Refraction through parallel slabs$q$,$q$COMP.SNT.PHYSICS$q$,$q$SRC.NCERT.SCIENCE$q$,$q$TEMP.STATIC$q$,80,90,100,60,57.75,0,0,0,0,$q${"answer_audit": {"authority": "DP_SOLVED_INTERNAL", "note": "Not an official UPSC key"}, "source_explanation_evidence": {"captured": true, "provider": "DP internal solved key", "text": "Concept: by Snell's law across parallel faces, $n_1\\sin\\theta_1=n_2\\sin\\theta_2=\\dots$, so the product $n\\sin\\theta$ is constant.\nThe light starts and ends in air, so the emergent angle equals the incident angle, $\\frac\\pi3$ (no total internal reflection occurs inside since $\\sin\\theta<1$ in every slab).\nAnswer: (c)"}}$q$::jsonb from b
union all
select b.id,72,null,$q$Consider three wires X, Y and Z of the same length such that the ratio of their conductivities is 1 : 2 : 3. Further, the cross-sectional area of wire Z is twice that of Y and the resistance of X is equal to the resistance of Z. What is the ratio of the resistance of Y to that of X?$q$,$q$1 : 1$q$,$q$3 : 1$q$,$q$2 : 1$q$,$q$1 : 2$q$,0.98,'{}'::text[],$q$NDA_II_2026_GK_072$q$,$q$Consider three wires X, Y and Z of the same length such that the ratio of their conductivities is 1 : 2 : 3. Further, the cross-sectional area of wire Z is twice that of Y and the resistance of X is equal to the resistance of Z. What is the ratio of the resistance of Y to that of X?$q$,$q$1 : 1$q$,$q$3 : 1$q$,$q$2 : 1$q$,$q$1 : 2$q$,$q$d27d436b76047a7a26f2b0784862a56031c0a7a7c77d9c6733940241f39a59c2$q$,$q$B$q$,'MODEL_ONLY',$q$dp-solved://NDA_2026_II_GAT_GK_SET_A$q$,null,$q$B$q$,$q$B$q$,false,$q$Science & Technology$q$,$q$Physics$q$,$q$Electricity & Electric Circuits$q$,$q$Resistance from conductivity and area$q$,'Knowledge',$q$Single MCQ$q$,$q$PATTERN.DIRECT$q$,$q$Concept: $R=\frac{\ell}{\sigma A}$.
Step 1: $R_X=R_Z\Rightarrow\frac1{1\cdot A_X}=\frac1{3\cdot2A_Y}\Rightarrow A_X=6A_Y$.
Step 2: $\frac{R_Y}{R_X}=\frac{1/(2A_Y)}{1/A_X}=\frac{A_X}{2A_Y}=3$.
Answer: (b) 3 : 1$q$,$q$NDA II 2026 General Ability Test Part B (English side)$q$,false,array['format:single_mcq','key:dp_solved'],$q$Static$q$,42.25,$q$Moderate$q$,0.97,0.85,0.85,false,'ENRICHED','INCLUDE',$q$Resistance from conductivity and area$q$,$q$COMP.SNT.PHYSICS$q$,$q$SRC.NCERT.SCIENCE$q$,$q$TEMP.STATIC$q$,80,90,100,60,57.75,0,0,0,0,$q${"answer_audit": {"authority": "DP_SOLVED_INTERNAL", "note": "Not an official UPSC key"}, "source_explanation_evidence": {"captured": true, "provider": "DP internal solved key", "text": "Concept: $R=\\frac{\\ell}{\\sigma A}$.\nStep 1: $R_X=R_Z\\Rightarrow\\frac1{1\\cdot A_X}=\\frac1{3\\cdot2A_Y}\\Rightarrow A_X=6A_Y$.\nStep 2: $\\frac{R_Y}{R_X}=\\frac{1/(2A_Y)}{1/A_X}=\\frac{A_X}{2A_Y}=3$.\nAnswer: (b) 3 : 1"}}$q$::jsonb from b
union all
select b.id,73,null,$q$Two point charges of 4 C and 16 C are kept at a distance of 0.18 m. A third point charge of 1 C is kept between them such that the potential energy of the system is minimum. What is the magnitude of the electric field at the 1 C charge?$q$,$q$0$q$,$q$(1/4πε₀)(1/9) N C⁻¹$q$,$q$(1/4πε₀)(2/9) N C⁻¹$q$,$q$(1/4πε₀)(1/18) N C⁻¹$q$,0.98,'{}'::text[],$q$NDA_II_2026_GK_073$q$,$q$Two point charges of 4 C and 16 C are kept at a distance of 0.18 m. A third point charge of 1 C is kept between them such that the potential energy of the system is minimum. What is the magnitude of the electric field at the 1 C charge?$q$,$q$0$q$,$q$(1/4πε₀)(1/9) N C⁻¹$q$,$q$(1/4πε₀)(2/9) N C⁻¹$q$,$q$(1/4πε₀)(1/18) N C⁻¹$q$,$q$c022aadc629490c76de26cf108294a64aa0204ed03e3ce2dc63179de18c2f392$q$,$q$A$q$,'MODEL_ONLY',$q$dp-solved://NDA_2026_II_GAT_GK_SET_A$q$,null,$q$A$q$,$q$A$q$,false,$q$Science & Technology$q$,$q$Physics$q$,$q$Electricity & Electric Circuits$q$,$q$Equilibrium point between two charges$q$,'Knowledge',$q$Single MCQ$q$,$q$PATTERN.DIRECT$q$,$q$Concept: the potential energy is minimum at the equilibrium point, where the net force (hence field) on the third charge is zero.
The point lies at 0.06 m from the 4 C charge ($\frac{x}{0.18-x}=\sqrt{\frac4{16}}$).
Field $=0$.
Answer: (a)$q$,$q$NDA II 2026 General Ability Test Part B (English side)$q$,false,array['format:single_mcq','key:dp_solved'],$q$Static$q$,42.25,$q$Moderate$q$,0.97,0.85,0.85,false,'ENRICHED','INCLUDE',$q$Equilibrium point between two charges$q$,$q$COMP.SNT.PHYSICS$q$,$q$SRC.NCERT.SCIENCE$q$,$q$TEMP.STATIC$q$,80,90,100,60,57.75,0,0,0,0,$q${"answer_audit": {"authority": "DP_SOLVED_INTERNAL", "note": "Not an official UPSC key"}, "source_explanation_evidence": {"captured": true, "provider": "DP internal solved key", "text": "Concept: the potential energy is minimum at the equilibrium point, where the net force (hence field) on the third charge is zero.\nThe point lies at 0.06 m from the 4 C charge ($\\frac{x}{0.18-x}=\\sqrt{\\frac4{16}}$).\nField $=0$.\nAnswer: (a)"}}$q$::jsonb from b
